# catsflap pubkey bastion — key -> principal map.
#
# One line per authorized client key:
#   <principal>  <keytype>  <key-base64>   [comment]
#
# - principal  the account the client becomes on the target host (and the cert's
#              principal). A login account of that name must exist on the host.
# - keytype    e.g. ssh-ed25519, ecdsa-sha2-nistp256, ssh-rsa
# - key-base64 the middle field of a public key. From `cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub`
#              (the "AAAA..." part), or paste the whole pubkey minus the comment.
#
# Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored. Edit and `docker compose up -d` to
# apply (the bastion recreates and re-reads this file).
#
# alice  ssh-ed25519  AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIExampleExampleExampleExampleExamplexxx  alice@laptop
# bob    ssh-ed25519  AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAnotherAnotherAnotherAnotherAnotheryyy  bob@desktop
